NOTES = [
    "Range: v7 288 frac ≈0.7 («والرابع: أنها نجسة») to v7 299 frac ≈0.8, just before «والذي يُصَبُّ عليه الماء بعد ما ذهب ثلثاه…», which the teacher only reads at 0:38:33 and defers (0:38:37–0:38:46); next lesson (2025-10-04) starts there. Not carded. Teacher's page refs (his copy): 1827 (0:00:08), 1830 (0:22:53), 1832 (0:30:11 and again 0:32:59).",
    "0:00:18–0:03:32 is a recap of the previous lesson; carded only as tamheed on card 1. In it (0:02:45–0:02:52) the teacher says for the 'other fuqaha' all intoxicants are khamr and a sip brings hadd; at 0:22:31–0:22:36 'jumhur: hadd for a sip'. Neither is in the matn/footnotes read here (only الكفاية ٩/٢٨, previous lesson, for Shafi'i); kept U-only and marked «استاد کے مطابق».",
    "Teacher's 'fatwa on Muhammad's view' (0:03:21, 0:19:41, 0:22:21–0:22:28, 0:31:05) is not in the matn/footnotes read; U-only. The book's «الأصح أنه يحد» (v7 297) is about hadd on intoxication from grain drinks, with the reason «الفساق يجتمعون عليه في زماننا»; the teacher gives that same reason for the fatwa on Muhammad (0:31:10). Carded separately.",
    "Card 2: teacher says pig and carrion/blood are 'not mal at all' (0:05:04, 0:05:14) — his comparison; the book only compares with «بيع الميتة». He says «کافر» for the debtor (0:06:04); book says «ذمّي» — card uses ذمی. Teacher says the price is امانت 'or by one view غصب' (0:05:56); book lists غصب first then أمانة; footnote attributes غصب to البردعي and أمانة to الطواويسي.",
    "Card 2/9: OCR v7 290 «لأن الحد بالقليل في النبيذ خاصة» and footnote «وهذا ليس بنبيذ» look like OCR for «النيء/بنيء» (the footnote says «الخمر لغة هو النيء من ماء العنب» – OCR «النبيذ»). OCR «جواز تحليلها» = «تخليلها». OCR v7 289 «وتضمن بها» = «وتَضِنّ بها». Card 4 start: OCR «النبيذ من ماء التمر»; previous file quoted «النيء». OCR v7 295 «إذ طبخ… طبخةً» for «إذا طبخ… أدنى طبخة».",
    "Card 3: teacher (0:09:41) says the 2/3-cooked (مثلث) is halal for Abu Hanifa; matn v7 297: Abu Hanifa and Abu Yusuf. Card 3 faida notes this.",
    "Card 4: teacher calls the توبيخ answer «دوسرا قول امام صاحب نے، صاحبِ ہدایہ نے» (0:12:45); matn introduces it with «وقيل». Card says «کتاب: وقيل». Teacher's reason for naqi' al-zabib (0:13:39: 'a small amount invites more') differs from the book's «وقد بينا المعنى من قبل», which البناية ١١/٤٢٤ explains as «رقيق ملذ مطرب»; card gives both, labelled. Teacher defines sakar as dates in raw water (0:11:43); matn «أي الرطب» (fresh dates) — noted on card from نتائج الأفكار ٩/٣٠.",
    "Card 5: at 0:14:55 the teacher gives both riwayat on the najasa of the three (ghaliza/khafifa), matching the matn; in the recap (0:17:48) he says flatly «باقیوں کی نجاست خفیفہ ہے». Card follows the matn (two riwayat). His gloss that 'sale is valid' means only that legal effects follow, 'not that it is halal' (0:15:28, 0:17:51) is his own explanation; labelled «استاد». Sale and daman are both AH's view per matn + البناية ١١/٤٢٥ («خلافاً لأبي يوسف ومحمد في البيع والإتلاف»).",
    "Card 6: teacher (0:20:08) says Imam Muhammad in الجامع الصغير stated it absolutely; the ruling is reported there as Abu Hanifa's («حلال عند أبي حنيفة»), so the card attributes the ruling to AH and the text to الجامع الصغير only. Teacher says Abu Yusuf's ten-day view was «میرے ہاں حرام» (0:21:43); matn «فإني أكرهه». Teacher lists AY's 'Muhammad-like' view (0:21:55) as separate from the ten-day view; matn: «وقوله الأول مثل قول محمد… إلا أنه تفرد بهذا الشرط» (one view), الكفاية ٩/٣٢ splits into two masa'il. Card follows the matn.",
    "Card 6: the teacher's 'some fuqaha say AH's permission is only for medicine/strength, not lahw' (0:19:17–0:19:33) — the matn states «إذا كان من غير لهو وطرب» as part of AH/AY's position (Qaduri, v7 296), not as 'some fuqaha'. Card keeps his wording labelled «استاد» with K7(296).",
    "Card 7: teacher calls the «غالب ظن / no lahw» condition one of two views from AH and speaks of «اضطراب» (0:23:49–0:24:25); in the matn (Qaduri) it is the stated condition, for AH and AY. Card gives the matn first, then the teacher's account labelled.",
    "Card 8: teacher names the guest «عبید اللہ ابن زیاد» (0:25:55); matn «ابن زياد», Kitab al-Athar footnote «ابن زيادة». Card says ابن زیاد. Teacher's two views from AH on cooked khalitayn (0:26:35: halal until intoxication / absolutely) are not in the matn; U-only labelled.",
    "Card 9: teacher slip 0:27:54 «حلال ہونے کے لیے شرط یہ ہے کہ وہ پکایا گیا نہ ہو» — he means «پکایا گیا ہو» (next lines 0:27:59–0:28:02: raw = haram among the four). Card gives the intended sense. Teacher calls «يشترط الطبخ / لا يشترط» 'two views of Imam sahib' (0:29:30); matn has «قيل… وقيل… وهو المذكور في الكتاب» (gloss: القدوري). Card quotes the matn. He calls «لا يحد» 'one view from Imam sahib' (0:30:31); matn «قيل» — footnote: الفقيه أبو جعفر; it matches the Jami' Saghir report (v7 293). Card shows both. Teacher's reason for «يحد» (0:30:51: permission only up to non-intoxicating amount) is his; the book's reason is Muhammad's narration + fussaq; both carded, labelled. Slip 0:31:33 «جو باقی چار ہیں» = the other (non-four) drinks. Lines 392–393 of the transcript (Muhammad: large amount intoxicates ⇒ intoxicant present; 'نئے بندے کو نشہ چڑھتا ہو') have no timestamps; cited via 0:29:54 only.",
    "Card 10: OCR v7 297 reads «وعن محمد مثل قولهما، وعنه: أنه توقف فيه» — two narrations; the common printed Hidaya also has «وعنه أنه كره ذلك» between them (OCR may have dropped it). Teacher (0:34:13) gives three: مکروہ، حلال، توقف, and says the راجح is مکروہ = حرام for Muhammad — not in the OCR/footnotes; U-only. Teacher's hadith 0:35:00 «جس کی ایک گھونٹ حرام ہے تو اس کا پورا مٹکا بھی حرام» inverts the matn («ما أسكر الجرة منه فالجرعة منه حرام»); card gives the matn wording. Teacher 0:36:03–0:36:11 «ایک قول کے مطابق نشہ ضروری ہے اور ایک قول کے مطابق نشہ چڑھنے کے بعد بھی وہ حرام نہیں ہوگا» is garbled (probably about hadd on the third category); not carded.",
    "Footnote citations converted page-first → vol/page as in earlier files: العناية ٢٩/٩→٩/٢٩, ٣١/٩, ٣٢/٩, ٣٣/٩, ٣٧/٩; الكفاية ٢٨/٩-٢٩→٩/٢٨–٢٩, ٢٩/٩, ٣٢/٩, ٣٣/٩, ٣٣/٩-٣٤, ٣٤/٩, ٣٤/٩-٣٥; نتائج الأفكار ٢٩/٩, ٣٠/٩, ٣١/٩, ٣١/٩-٣٢, ٣٧/٩; البناية ٤٠٧/١١, ٤٠٨/١١-٤٠٩, ٤١٤/١١, ٤١٦/١١, ٤٢١/١١, ٤٢٤/١١, ٤٢٥/١١, ٤٢٨/١١, ٤٣٦/١١, ٤٣٨/١١, ٤٤١/١١, ٤٤٦/١١ → ١١/…; نصب الراية printed as «٤ / ٣٠١», «٤ / ٣٠٥ - ٣٠٦», «٤ / ٣٠٦». Bare «(البناية)/(الكفاية)/(العناية)» glosses cited by name only. Hadith takhrij cited as «حاشیہ ص ٢٩٥/٢٩٨». The footnote «ما رويناه… [البناية ٣١/٩]» (v7 291) has an odd vol/page for البناية (probably العناية ٩/٣١); not cited. The footnote at v7 299 «[العناية ٣٧/١١]» is also odd; not cited.",
]
